{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T21:20:19.362Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"436e44ca2d204a1ee603915a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1656"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1656: a transaction-owned finalization step for commitItemMutations, so importers keep rollback under the GH-1591 ownership guard"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Since GH-1591 (pm-pllp78) commitItemMutations compensates only effects it can prove a step owns. pm-github's importer finalizes exact GitHub source-lifecycle fields (persistImportFidelity, a raw mutateItem op 'import') from the committing transition observer. That event is outside every step's ownership proof, so a failure after finalization reports transaction_partial_mutation and leaves a half-imported tracker. The bulk union accepts only create, update, close and release, and update cannot write native lifecycle fields (closed_at, completed_at) or arbitrary extension fields. Need a journaled step the transaction owns, with its own snapshot and compensation, without weakening the ownership guard. Related to transaction inspection (pm-gh1597)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["extensions","gh:1656","importers","sdk","transactions"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-03T21:20:19.362Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T21:20:19.362Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":480},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"commitItemMutations accepts a finalization step (field-level document patch or SDK-applied finalize step) that is journaled, attributed to the transaction and compensated by restore exactly like an update step; The GH-1656 reproduction (update step plus finalization, then a failure in the committing observer) restores the item to its pre-batch document with no transaction_partial_mutation; An unowned write by another writer between apply and compensation still refuses with transaction_partial_mutation (negative control); The step is exposed through the public SDK types, docs/SDK.md and the SDK surface snapshot; recovery of an interrupted journal re-applies or adopts the finalization deterministically"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-9rgaal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1597","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:20:19.362Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-pllp78","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:20:19.362Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-xm7c","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:20:19.362Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-y9hq","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:20:19.362Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-03T21:20:19.362Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Duplicate check: the create-time detector matched pm-pllp78 (GH-1591, the ownership guard fix, closed). This item is not a recurrence of that defect: the guard stays as shipped, and this asks for a new journaled step type the guard can attribute. pm search for 'finalization commitItemMutations' found only the closed bulk-helper lineage (pm-xm7c, pm-y9hq)."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"7ecafb90fbd2f66bd6ff3a08a3f46f203b1492ba9250d17d1d615da2e736f29e","item_hash_version":3,"message":"File GH-1656","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"48fb2cf8b430a359b36c8fd2606e825dfea822f2c16d0eeb3e8d07984d029ce1"}
